window.addressFieldDescriptions={address:{address_line_1:"The first line of the formatted address.",address_line_2:"The second line of the formatted address.",address_line_3:"The third line of the formatted address, when supplied by the address dataset.",locality:"The locality, such as a town or city, associated with the address.",region:"The region, state, province or county associated with the address.",postal_code:"The postal code, ZIP code or equivalent postal identifier for the address.",country:"The country associated with the address.",country_iso_2:"The two-letter ISO 3166-1 country code for the address.",country_iso_3:"The three-letter ISO 3166-1 country code for the address."},components:{language:"The language and country variant used to return the address components.",country_name:"The full country name associated with the address.",country_iso_3:"The three-letter ISO 3166-1 country code for the address.",country_iso_2:"The two-letter ISO 3166-1 country code for the address.",country_iso_numeric:"The numeric ISO 3166-1 country code for the address.",full_name:"The complete value for this address component.",primary:"The primary value used for this address component.",building_number:"The number identifying the building or premises.",company_name:"The company or organization name associated with the address.",street:"The street component of the address.",name:"The name of the current address component.",type:"The type or classification of the current address component.",code:"The code identifying the current administrative or geographic component.",description:"A human-readable description of the current administrative or geographic component.",town:"The town associated with the address.",premise:"The building, house or property identifier for the address.",premise_number:"The numeric identifier of the premise.",sub_building:"The unit, flat, apartment or other sub-building identifier.",building_name:"The name of the building or property.",organization:"The business or organization associated with the address.",thoroughfare:"The street or thoroughfare on which the address is located.",dependent_thoroughfare:"A secondary thoroughfare used to further identify the address.",dependent_locality:"A locality subordinate to the primary locality.",double_dependent_locality:"A locality subordinate to a dependent locality.",locality:"The locality, town or city associated with the address.",post_town:"The postal town used for delivery.",administrative_area:"The administrative area, state, province, county or region.",postal_code:"The postal code or equivalent postal identifier.",country:"The country associated with the address.",dpid:"A unique 8-digit numeric code assigned by Australia Post to every deliverable address in Australia. The DPID uniquely identifies the physical delivery point within the PAF (Postal Address File) and is used by Australia Post systems to route mail and parcels to the correct location.",udprn:"A permanent 8-digit numeric identifier assigned by Royal Mail to every delivery point in the UK PAF. The UDPRN remains stable even if an address is renumbered or renamed, providing a reliable long-term key for linking address records.",gnaf_pid:"A permanent, government-assigned identifier for each address in the GNAF dataset maintained by PSMA Australia (now Geoscape). Unlike street addresses, a GNAF PID never changes when a property is renumbered or renamed, making it a stable key for linking address records across datasets over time.",hin:"An internal address identifier used within the Australia Post PAF dataset. It uniquely references a specific delivery point record within the PAF, complementing the DPID as a cross-reference key when working with Australia Post data.",address_id:"An internal identifier assigned by the Experian dataset to this specific address record. It provides a stable reference for address records within Experian's address database and can be used to retrieve or update a specific record without re-running a full address search.",delivery_type:"Classifies the address as either Residential (R) or Business (B) based on the PAF and GNAF datasets. This classification reflects the primary use of the premises as recorded in postal and geocoded address data.",address_type:"Describes the structural classification of the address—for example, whether it is a standard street address, a rural address, a post office box, a locked bag, or a care-of address. This helps systems apply the correct formatting, routing rules, and data requirements for each address category.",sort_plan:"The Australia Post sort plan number identifies the machine-sortable grouping for this delivery point. It is used by Australia Post's automated letter sorting equipment to assign mail to the correct delivery walk and round.",delivery_barcode:"A machine-readable Code 128 barcode generated by the Experian Address Validation API for this delivery point. It encodes the address's sort plan and DPID into a format that Australia Post's automated letter sorting equipment can scan directly.",paf_key:"The Royal Mail PAF Address Key is a unique alphanumeric reference for the address within the PAF dataset. It complements the UDPRN and is used by Royal Mail APIs and licensees to uniquely reference and retrieve a specific PAF record.",paths:{building:"The building component identifies a named or numbered building associated with the address. It may include the complete building value and its primary identifier.","locality.region":"The region or administrative area containing the locality, including its name, dataset code, and geographic or administrative description when supplied.","locality.sub_region":"A geographic or administrative area within the locality's region, including its name, code, and description when supplied.","postal_code.full_name":"The complete postal code as formatted for the address by the selected country dataset.","postal_code.primary":"The primary postal code value returned for the address. It may contain the complete postal code when the dataset does not return separate parts.","street.full_name":"The complete street or thoroughfare name as formatted for the address, including its type when the dataset provides one.","street.name":"The name of the street or thoroughfare, separate from its type when those parts are returned individually.","street.type":"The street or thoroughfare type, such as Street or Road, when returned separately from its name.","locality.full_name":"The complete name of the locality associated with the address.","locality.primary":"The primary locality value used to identify the address's delivery locality.","locality.name":"The name of the locality, such as a town, city, suburb, or post town.","locality.type":"The locality classification, when the selected dataset supplies one.","locality.region.name":"The name of the region or administrative area containing the address.","locality.region.code":"The dataset's code for the region or administrative area containing the address.","locality.region.description":"A description of the region's administrative or geographic classification.","locality.sub_region.name":"The name of the sub-region within the address's region.","locality.sub_region.code":"The dataset's code for the sub-region within the address's region.","locality.sub_region.description":"A description of the sub-region's administrative or geographic classification.","organization.department_name":"The department within the organization associated with the address.","locality.district":"A locality subdivision used to further identify the address. Depending on the country dataset, this may represent a dependent locality, urbanization, delivery-area installation, lobby, geographic town, or settlement.","sub_building.door":"A door identifier or designation associated with the sub-building, used to further identify an entry or unit within the building.",additional_elements:"Supplementary address components returned by the dataset in addition to the standard component hierarchy. The available elements vary by country and dataset.","additional_elements.locality.sub_region":"A supplementary geographic or administrative subdivision within the locality. It can include country-specific county information.","additional_elements.locality.sub_region.administrative_county":"The administrative county associated with the address, representing its county-level administrative area.","additional_elements.locality.sub_region.traditional_county":"The traditional or historic county associated with the address, which may differ from its current administrative county.","locality.town.name":"The name of the town associated with the address.","building.full_name":"The complete building name or identifier returned for the address.","building.primary":"The primary building name or identifier returned for the address."}},metadata:{address_info:"Additional address identification and classification information returned for the validated address.",identifier:"Identifiers used to reference the address in the selected postal dataset.",dpid:"A unique 8-digit numeric code assigned by Australia Post to every deliverable address in Australia. The DPID uniquely identifies the physical delivery point within the PAF (Postal Address File) and is used by Australia Post systems to route mail and parcels to the correct location.",hin:"An internal address identifier used within the Australia Post PAF dataset. It uniquely references a specific delivery point record within the PAF, complementing the DPID as a cross-reference key when working with Australia Post data.",barcode:"A machine-readable Code 128 barcode generated by Experian Address Validation for the delivery point. It encodes the address's sort plan and DPID so postal sorting equipment can route mail to the correct delivery walk.",delivery_barcode:"A machine-readable Code 128 barcode generated by Experian Address Validation for the delivery point. It encodes the address's sort plan and DPID so postal sorting equipment can route mail to the correct delivery walk.",delivery_point_barcode:"A machine-readable Code 128 barcode generated by Experian Address Validation for the delivery point. It encodes the address's sort plan and DPID so postal sorting equipment can route mail to the correct delivery walk.",sort_plan:"The Australia Post sort plan number identifies the machine-sortable grouping for this delivery point and is used to assign mail to the correct delivery walk and round.",sort_plan_number:"The Australia Post sort plan number identifies the machine-sortable grouping for this delivery point and is used to assign mail to the correct delivery walk and round.",gnaf_pid:"A permanent, government-assigned identifier for each address in the GNAF dataset. It remains stable when a property is renumbered or renamed, making it a reliable key for linking address records.",address_id:"An internal identifier assigned by the Experian dataset to this address record. It provides a stable reference for retrieving or updating the record.",address_type:"Describes the structural classification of the address, such as a street address, rural address, post office box, locked bag, or care-of address.",paf_key:"The Royal Mail PAF Address Key is a unique alphanumeric reference for the address within the PAF dataset.",udprn:"A permanent 8-digit numeric identifier assigned by Royal Mail to every delivery point in the UK PAF.",paf_address_key:"The Royal Mail PAF Address Key is a unique alphanumeric reference for the address within the PAF dataset.",dps:"The Delivery Point Suffix used with the postcode and address identifiers to identify the delivery point.",number_of_households:"The number of households present at the address for Royal Mail Multiple Residence and Not Yet Built addresses.",umrrn:"Royal Mail's Unique Multiple Residence Reference Number, an eight-digit code linked to UDPRNs in the Multiple Residence dataset.",address_classification:"Classification information describing the type of address.",delivery_type:"Classifies the validated address as residential or business, based on the address dataset's information about the delivery point.",match_type:"Describes how the submitted address was matched to the reference dataset during validation. Examples include Full Match, Alias Match, and Partial Match.",match_confidence:"A categorical or numeric score expressing the system's confidence in the accuracy of the address match. Higher confidence indicates a clear, unambiguous match against a single reference record.",confidence:"Indicates how confidently the submitted address was matched to the reference data. Values describe the validation outcome, such as a verified match, interaction required, partial match, multiple matches, or no matches.",global_address_key:"The unique global key used to identify the validated address.",dataset:"The reference dataset used to validate the address.",format:"The format used to return the address.",language:"The language used for the returned address.",address_key:"The key used to identify the address in the selected dataset.",postal_code:"The postal code or equivalent postal identifier.",country:"The country associated with the address."},enrichment:{premium_location_insight:"Premium Location Insight provides additional property-level location data, including geocodes, building grid references, access points, and local time-zone information.",gbr_location_essential:"GBR Location Essential provides core UK location attributes for the validated address, including coordinates, match level, and UK property identifiers.",geocodes:"Geocodes provides latitude and longitude coordinates and the match level for the address.",geocodes_building_xy:"Building XY provides projected X and Y coordinates for the address or building location.",geocodes_access:"Access Points provides coordinates for the vehicle or pedestrian access point to the property.",time:"Time provides the local time-zone details for the address, including time-zone names, offsets, and solar times.",reference_time:"The current time zone information for the specified address, including offsets and sunrise/sunset times. Values are based on the current timestamp, so sunrise and sunset times vary depending on the date of the request.",time_transition:"An array of daylight saving time transition periods for the specified address. Each transition includes start and end times in ISO 8601 format.",latitude:"The latitude of the specified address, expressed in decimal degrees.",longitude:"The longitude of the specified address, expressed in decimal degrees.",udprn:"A permanent 8-digit numeric identifier assigned by Royal Mail to every delivery point in the UK PAF.",uprn:"The Unique Property Reference Number assigned to the property in the UK address reference data.",x_coordinate:"Easting (X-axis) value in the grid reference system.",y_coordinate:"Northing (Y-axis) value in the grid reference system.",address_level_latitude:"The latitude coordinate at address level.",address_level_longitude:"The longitude coordinate at address level.",street_level_latitude:"The latitude coordinate at street level.",street_level_longitude:"The longitude coordinate at street level.",locality_level_latitude:"The latitude coordinate at locality level.",locality_level_longitude:"The longitude coordinate at locality level.",centroid_of_property_latitude:"The latitude coordinate for the property centroid.",centroid_of_property_longitude:"The longitude coordinate for the property centroid.",front_of_property_latitude:"The latitude coordinate at the front of the property.",front_of_property_longitude:"The longitude coordinate at the front of the property.",geocode_level:"Indicates the precision level at which the geocoordinate was assigned to this address - typically Property, Street, Locality, or District. A property-level geocode places the coordinate at the specific building; lower levels indicate less precision.",match_level:"Indicates the precision of the geocode for the specified address.",lga:"The Local Government Area (LGA) in which the address is located, including both the LGA name and code. LGAs are the primary unit of local government in Australia.",sa1:"The ABS (Australian Bureau of Statistics) Statistical Area Level 1 code for this address. SA1 is the smallest unit in the ABS geographic structure, containing approximately 200-800 persons.",meshblock:"The ABS Meshblock code for this address. Meshblocks are the smallest geographic unit in the ABS hierarchy, containing approximately 30-60 dwellings.",geocode_reliability:"A code and description indicating the source and method used to derive the geocoordinate - for example, GPS survey, photogrammetry, or interpolation.",planimetric_accuracy:"The estimated horizontal positional accuracy of the geocoordinate, expressed in metres. This indicates how closely the coordinate is expected to match the true ground position of the address.",street_pid:"The GNAF Persistent Identifier for the street on which this address is located. It remains stable regardless of street name changes or renumbering.",locality_pid:"The GNAF Persistent Identifier for the suburb or locality of this address. It links the address to all GNAF locality attributes including boundary polygons.",primary_pid:"The GNAF Persistent Identifier uniquely assigned to this specific address point. This is the master stable key for the address within the entire GNAF dataset.",parcel_id:"Links the address to its legal land parcel (lot and plan number) within the cadastre. It enables connection between the postal address and the legal description of the property in title records.",geocode_level_code:"The code identifying the level of the returned geocode.",geocode_level_description:"A description of the level of the returned geocode.",geocode_type_code:"The code identifying the type of geocode returned.",geocode_type_description:"A description of the type of geocode returned.",confidence_level_code:"The code representing the confidence level of the enrichment result.",confidence_level_description:"A description of the confidence level of the enrichment result.",name:"The name returned by the enrichment dataset.",address:"The address associated with the enrichment result.",time_zone_id:"The IANA time zone ID for the specified address (for example, Europe/London).",generic:"The generic time zone name for the specified address (for example, United Kingdom Time).",standard:"The standard time zone name for the specified address (for example, Greenwich Mean Time).",daylight:"The daylight saving time zone name for the specified address (for example, British Summer Time).",tag:"The current time zone tag (for example, BST or GMT).",standard_offset:"The standard time offset from UTC for the specified address at the current timestamp.",daylight_savings:"The daylight saving time offset from UTC for the specified address at the current timestamp.",sunrise:"The local time of sunrise for the specified address on the current date, expressed in ISO 8601 format.",sunset:"The local time of sunset for the specified address on the current date, expressed in ISO 8601 format.",utc_start:"The UTC start time of the time zone transition period.",utc_end:"The UTC end time of the time zone transition period.",geocodes_group:"Standard WGS84 latitude/longitude geocoordinates for this address from the Premium Location Insight dataset. Includes a match level indicating the precision of the geocode placement.",building_xy_group:"Easting (X) and Northing (Y) coordinates in a national grid projection, representing the centroid of the building footprint.",access_points_group:"Geocoordinates marking the vehicle or pedestrian access points to the property, typically the driveway entrance or gate location on the street.",time_zone_group:"The local time zone for this address including the IANA time zone ID, standard and daylight saving time offsets, and DST transition dates."},match_info:{match_type:"Describes how the submitted address matched the reference data.",match_confidence:"Indicates the confidence of the address match.",postcode_action:"The action applied to the validated address's postal code: none means no action was taken; ok means the supplied postal code was already correct; added means a postal code was added; corrected means the supplied postal code was corrected.",address_action:"The action applied to the validated address: none means the supplied address was not matched; reformatted means part or all of it was reformatted; enhanced means information was added without significant information being removed; corrected means the existing address was corrected.",generic_info:"A collection of strings for generic validation flags. These flags describe address-processing conditions such as altered or truncated output, unexpected element order, partial matches, unmatched input, or validation timeouts.",0:"The first generic validation flag in the collection. Its value identifies an address-processing or matching condition.",1:"The second generic validation flag in the collection. Its value identifies an address-processing or matching condition.",paths:{"generic_info.0":"The first generic validation flag in the collection. Its value identifies an address-processing or matching condition.","generic_info.1":"The second generic validation flag in the collection. Its value identifies an address-processing or matching condition."}},email:{email:"The email address submitted for validation.",confidence:"The overall deliverability verdict returned by the Experian Email Validation API. It is based on syntax checking, domain MX record lookup, and live SMTP mailbox verification.",verbose_output:"The detailed diagnostic code returned by the Experian Email Validation API. It provides the precise reason behind the confidence result and supports granular data-quality decisions.",verbose_output_status:"The meaning of this verbose output value.",type:"Classifies the email domain as a Business (corporate) or Personal (consumer) domain.",domain_type:"Classifies the email domain as a Business (corporate) or Personal (consumer) domain.",normalised:"The standardised form of the submitted email address after applying corrections such as case normalization, removal of unnecessary dots, and resolution of known provider aliases.",mx:"The result of checking the domain's MX (Mail Exchange) DNS records to confirm that the domain is configured to receive email.",definition:"A human-readable explanation of the email validation diagnostic result.",confidence_statuses:{verified:"Mailbox confirmed deliverable via live SMTP check. The address exists, the domain has valid MX records, and the server accepted the address.",undeliverable:"The address does not exist, the mailbox is disabled or full, or the mail server explicitly rejected the address.",illegitimate:"The address is a seed, spam trap, black hole, technical role account, or belongs to an inactive domain. It is not a genuine personal or business address.",disposable:"The domain is administered by a disposable or temporary email provider. These addresses are often used to bypass registration requirements.",unreachable:"The domain has no active mail servers, or SMTP verification could not complete because of a timeout, greylisting, or temporary block.",acceptall:"The domain accepts all incoming email regardless of whether the specific mailbox exists, so individual mailbox existence cannot be confirmed.",timeout:"The validation request timed out because the host domain did not respond in time. The result is inconclusive.",relaydenied:"The result was validated at the incorrect mail exchanger, or the mail server refused the SMTP relay verification request.",unknown:"Validation completed but a definitive result could not be determined because the mail server did not respond conclusively."},verbose_output_statuses:{verified:"Mailbox confirmed deliverable via live SMTP handshake. The address exists, the domain has valid MX records, and the server accepted the address.",mailboxdoesnotexist:"The specific mailbox does not exist at the domain. The SMTP server explicitly rejected the address.",mailboxdisabled:"The mailbox exists but has been suspended or disabled by the provider or the account owner.",syntaxfailure:"The email address does not conform to valid RFC 5321/5322 syntax. It cannot be a real email address in its current form.",illegitimate:"The domain or address pattern is associated with known fraudulent, abusive, or bot-generated activity.",localpartspamtrap:"The local part of the address matches a known spam trap address pattern used by anti-spam organisations to identify unsolicited senders.",mailboxfull:"The mailbox exists and is reachable, but it is over its storage quota and is unable to accept new mail.",unreachable:"The domain has valid MX records but the SMTP connection could not complete because of a server timeout, greylisting, temporary connection refusal, or anti-verification throttling.",roleaccount:"The address is a functional or role-based account (for example info@, support@, noreply@, or admin@). These are monitored by teams, not individuals.",typodomain:"The domain appears to contain a common typo (for example gnail.com instead of gmail.com). The address may be a genuine user mistake.",disposable:"The domain belongs to a temporary or disposable email provider (for example Mailinator or Guerrilla Mail).",acceptall:"The domain accepts all incoming email regardless of whether the specific mailbox exists. Individual mailbox existence cannot be confirmed.",timeout:"The SMTP connection attempt timed out before the mail server returned a definitive response. The result is inconclusive.",relaydenied:"The mail server refused the SMTP relay verification request. This commonly occurs when servers block external validation probes.",profanity:"The local part of the address contains profane, offensive, or inappropriate terms.",unknown:"Validation completed but a definitive result could not be determined. This may occur for restricted networks, unusual server configurations, or addresses outside normal validation patterns."}},phone:{number:"The phone number submitted for validation.",validated_phone_number:"The validated phone number returned by the Phone Validation API.",formatted_phone_number:"The phone number formatted according to the requested output format and country.",phone_type:"The line type classification for this phone number, such as Mobile, Fixed Line, VoIP, Premium Rate, Toll-Free, or Unknown.",confidence:"The real-time network reachability status returned by the Experian Phone Validation API. It is determined by a live HLR (Home Location Register) lookup against the carrier network.",ported_date:"The date on which the mobile number was most recently ported between carriers.",disposable_number:"Indicates whether the number is associated with a disposable or temporary phone-number service.",operator_name:"The name of the network operator currently hosting the phone number. For ported numbers, this is the current carrier.",network_status:"The current status of the phone number on the network, such as Active, Inactive, Absent, or Dead.",country_name:"The country in which the phone number is registered, based on its country code and national numbering plan.",home_network_identity:"The Mobile Country Code (MCC) and Mobile Network Code (MNC) of the network where the phone number is currently registered.",country_prefix:"The international calling code of the country where the phone number is currently registered.",country_iso:"The 3-letter ISO code of the country where the phone number is currently registered.",original_operator_name:"The name of the network operator with which the phone number was initially registered. Operator names may change over time due to acquisitions, mergers, or regulatory updates.",original_network_status:"The status of the network where the phone number was originally registered.",original_home_network_identity:"The Mobile Country Code (MCC) and Mobile Network Code (MNC) of the network where the phone number was originally registered.",original_country_prefix:"The international calling code of the country where the phone number was originally registered.",original_country_name:"The name of the country where the phone number was originally registered.",original_country_iso:"The 3-letter ISO code of the country where the phone number was originally registered.",is_ported:"Indicates whether the phone number has been ported to a different network.",cache_value_days:"The requested number of days to look back in the cache for this phone number.",date_cached:"The last date this phone number was checked.",email_to_sms_address:"The email address format that can be used to send a message to the mobile number through the carrier's SMS-to-email gateway.",email_to_mms_address:"The email address that can be used to send MMS messages to this phone number.",confidence_statuses:{verified:"The number format is valid and the number has been confirmed active via a live network lookup. The handset is reachable and can receive calls and SMS.",absent:"The number format is valid and verified via network lookup, but the handset is not currently available—for example, it is switched off, out of range, or has call barring active.",dead:"The network has confirmed the number is permanently disconnected and will not receive calls or SMS. It cannot be reactivated.",teleservicenotprovisioned:"The number is assigned to a SIM card that is not permitted to make or receive telephone calls. This is typically a data-only SIM, such as a mobile broadband or IoT device.",unverified:"The supplied number format is invalid and could not be verified. It does not conform to expected format rules for the specified country.",nocoverage:"The live network status could not be detected. The carrier may not support real-time HLR lookup for this number range.",unknown:"The number format is valid but could not be verified via a live network lookup. This is common for international numbers or restricted network ranges."}},fallback:"This field provides information about the validation result."};